RandR rates from the kernel's mode table (ZZ9KIOC_GETMODES/SETMODEHZ, amix-gate 32e04d7):
every size gets the rates of its kernel rows (whole Hz: 1080p 61 and 51), the
current one from the CURRENT row; a new rate at the same size changes the timing
only (same stride and pixels, no clear, no exposures).  An older kernel answers
EINVAL: 60 Hz alone, as before.

